WEBVTT

00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:04.320
Welcome to our final topic in lesson five.

00:00:04.320 --> 00:00:08.040
Your team just finished a massive project

00:00:08.040 --> 00:00:11.000
and everyone is exhausted.

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:12.200
What's your next move?

00:00:13.080 --> 00:00:16.720
In sports, the post-game recovery protocol

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.740
is as important as the pre-game warmup.

00:00:20.740 --> 00:00:23.380
In business, it should be no different.

00:00:23.380 --> 00:00:27.540
Facilitating team recovery is the intentional process

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:31.380
of helping your team recharge and reset

00:00:31.380 --> 00:00:34.180
after a period of intense effort.

00:00:34.180 --> 00:00:38.020
It prevents burnout, reinforces the value of their work,

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:40.340
and prepares them for the next challenge.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:43.180
After a grueling quarter end,

00:00:43.180 --> 00:00:45.060
a manager didn't immediately launch

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.140
into planning for the next quarter.

00:00:47.140 --> 00:00:50.460
She dedicated the first team meeting of the new quarter

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:54.080
entirely to retrospective and recovery.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:58.840
They celebrated the wins, discussed the lessons learned,

00:00:58.840 --> 00:01:02.520
and she gave everyone an extra half a day to recharge.

00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:06.480
The team came back energized and focused.

00:01:06.480 --> 00:01:09.780
At Velvet Suite, we practice the 90-Day Way.

00:01:09.780 --> 00:01:13.300
And at the end of every quarter, we give a reset day,

00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:17.440
which is a half day to focus on a few things.

00:01:17.440 --> 00:01:20.120
Collective reflection, recharge,

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:21.960
and putting together our thoughts

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:26.360
around what will make the next 90-Day Way even stronger.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:29.720
Your play is to plan a recovery protocol.

00:01:29.720 --> 00:01:32.080
Look ahead at your team's calendar.

00:01:32.080 --> 00:01:35.160
After the next big deadline or project launch,

00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:37.640
what is the one small thing you can do

00:01:37.640 --> 00:01:40.740
to facilitate team recovery?

00:01:40.740 --> 00:01:42.360
I want you to schedule it now.

00:01:43.320 --> 00:01:46.320
Your team is facing a mandatory crunch time

00:01:46.320 --> 00:01:48.280
to meet a critical deadline.

00:01:48.280 --> 00:01:50.480
You can't change the workload,

00:01:50.560 --> 00:01:53.600
you can lead their recovery.

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:57.160
How do you proactively plan for a post-deadline recovery

00:01:57.160 --> 00:02:00.780
to prevent burnout and acknowledge their effort?

00:02:00.780 --> 00:02:03.200
Turn to the team's recovery protocols drill

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.440
in your playbook.

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:06.600
It provides a template for planning

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:09.040
a post-crunch recovery strategy

00:02:09.040 --> 00:02:13.380
that rebuilds energy and reinforces trust.

00:02:13.380 --> 00:02:16.240
This concludes lesson five.

00:02:16.240 --> 00:02:18.880
You are now equipped with strategies

00:02:18.880 --> 00:02:22.280
to manage your own energy and to lead your team

00:02:22.280 --> 00:02:25.040
in a way that ensures sustainability,

00:02:25.040 --> 00:02:29.360
long-term performance, and health and vitality.

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:33.600
And our final lesson will focus on the victory lap,

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:36.260
integrating your learnings and plannings

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:38.240
for your next season of leadership.

00:02:38.240 --> 00:02:39.320
I'll see you there.

00:02:39.320 --> 00:02:40.980
You
